agrange's method can be used to reduce the quadratic form $Q(x)=4{x}_{1}^{2}+8{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}$ to the canonical form given below. \n\n$$\n\\boxed{}\\,{y}_{1}^{2}-5{y}_{2}^{2},\\,{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{2}={x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what is missing from the blank spaces?" 13194139536003 true] [17592186379061 1113 #uuid "114299ac-5cb6-5ace-82c7-9724e64c9935" 13194139536003 true] [17592186379061 1145 "We apply Lagrange's method as follows:\n\nFirst, we group ${x}_{1}^{2}$-term with all cross-product terms that contain ${x}_{1}$ and factor out the coefficient of ${x}_{1}^{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =4{x}_{1}^{2}+8{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =(4{x}_{1}^{2}+8{x}_{1}{x}_{2})-{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =4({x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2})-{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we complete the square inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4({x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2})-{x}_{2}^{2} & =4([{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}]-{x}_{2}^{2})-{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =4(({x}_{1}+{x}_{2})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2})-{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we simplify the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(({x}_{1}+{x}_{2})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2})-{x}_{2}^{2} & =4({x}_{1}+{x}_{2})^{2}-4{x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =4({x}_{1}+{x}_{2})^{2}-5{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the canonical form is\n\n$$\n4{y}_{1}^{2}-5{y}_{2}^{2},\\,{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}={x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}={x}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the missing parts are as follows:\n\n$\\,$ $4\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}.$" 13194139536003 true] [17592186379062 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379063 13194139536003 true] [17592186379062 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379064 13194139536003 true] [17592186379062 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379065 13194139536003 true] [17592186379062 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379066 13194139536003 true] [17592186379062 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379067 13194139536003 true] [17592186379062 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536003 true] 