grange's method as follows:\n\nFirst, we group ${x}_{1}^{2}$-term with all cross-product terms that contain ${x}_{1}$ and factor out the coefficient of ${x}_{1}^{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =9{x}_{1}^{2}-18{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+16{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =(9{x}_{1}^{2}-18{x}_{1}{x}_{2})+16{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =9({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2})+16{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we complete the square inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2})+16{x}_{2}^{2} & =9([{x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}]-{x}_{2}^{2})+16{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =9(({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2})+16{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we simplify the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9(({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2})+16{x}_{2}^{2} & =9({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})^{2}-9{x}_{2}^{2}+16{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =9({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})^{2}+7{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the canonical form is\n\n$$\n9{y}_{1}^{2}+7{y}_{2}^{2},\\,{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}={x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}={x}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the missing parts are as follows:\n\n$\\,$ $9\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}.$" 13194139536003 true] [17592186379069 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379070 13194139536003 true] [17592186379069 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379071 13194139536003 true] [17592186379069 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379072 13194139536003 true] [17592186379069 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379073 13194139536003 true] [17592186379069 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379074 13194139536003 true] [17592186379069 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536003 true] [17592186379069 1041 "selection" 13194139536003 true] [17592186379069 1104 #edb/ref 17592186379070 13194139536003 true] [17592186379069 1110 #uuid "60347550-5557-5b74-b1fd-70e810ae5ac1" 13194139536003 true] [17592186379070 1034 "$9$ and ${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}$" 13194139536003 true] [17592186379070 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536003 true] [17592186379070 1111 #uuid "a61c089e-855c-5bc9-b034-517a3d1b718f" 13194139536003 true] [17592186379071 103